Patch 2504: RES_SCALE takes any factor from 1 to 4, not only whole ones: 1.25 = 900p, 1.5 = 1080p, 2.5 = 1800p.

Scales become floats; resource sizes are the guest size times the scale, rounded (RSZ). A new target's guest contents
are widened by nearest texel at any factor; the depth copy of a scaled depth surface samples at the scale ratio. Whole
factors give the same sizes as patch 2503.

Tested (US disc, quick Free Battle route, CPU boost on): RES_SCALE=1.5 renders at 1920x1080, picture right, Free Battle
29.87 flips/s (bench/feature/2026-11-09_1839-res15b). Attract demo at 1.5 looks right (Allen's coat grey,
2026-11-09_1803-res15). Runs with the boost off were all ~20.8 flips/s, the fix build too (2026-11-09_1833-syscheck).

